# VHS hidden and shown again (X-Background=run): the camera is released while hidden (nothing drawn) and opened
# again on show (brief 3.3 rule 5). M3: a hide during a recording finishes the scene first (brief 13, owner answer
# D37: finish and save, hide with the camera released, come back live); a close during a recording too (the file is
# finished in the teardown, after the quit).
title VHS hidden and shown again (X-Background=run): the camera released and reopened, a recording finished
sizes 800x480
lifecycle
env VHS_FAKE 1
env VHS_SOC bcm2837
env VHS_FORMAT rgb565
env VHS_CLOCK_SYNCED 0
env VHS_FAKE_MIC tone

wait 1500
shot 01-live
expect text "1920x1080  30 fps"
key r
wait 2000
shot 02-recording
expect text "Photo now"
hide
wait 800
expect hidden
expect nowrite
show
wait 1500
expect visible
expect repaint
shot 03-shown
expect text "1920x1080  30 fps"
expect text "Photo | Video"
expect notext "Photo now"
key r
wait 1500
expect text "Photo now"
close
expect quit
